## Failure modes documented by this scenario
------------------------------------------------------------
1. Impossible instance family / no matching capacity.
   A NodePool with karpenter.k8s.aws/instance-family=doesnotexist
   is valid YAML but can never launch. Karpenter returns an empty
   candidate set; pods stay Pending; events show
   "filtered 1000+ instance types down to 0".

2. VPC quota exceeded (the eu-central-1 blocker).
   Account 050451381948 hit the per-region VPC ceiling with
   5 VPCs already in eu-central-1. kops update cluster --yes
   failed with VpcLimitExceeded. Lab moved to us-west-2.

3. Control-plane API timeout (the us-west-2 blocker).
   The kOps-managed NLB control-plane endpoint never became
   reachable; kubectl calls hang / time out from the operator
   workstation. This script tolerates those failures so the
   log captures every failure mode in one place.

4. Missing IAM permission.
   A NodeClaim stuck in NotLaunched with an AccessDenied event
   from AWS indicates the Karpenter controller role lacks
   iam:PassRole on the EC2NodeClass instanceProfile.

